    <section id="about">
      <h2>About</h2>
      <p>I work at <a href="https://thebusinessofcities.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Business of Cities</a>, a cities research and strategy firm, where I build tools and produce publications to help cities understand themselves from an outside-in perspective.</p>
      <p>I studied on a Morehead-Cain scholarship at UNC Chapel Hill, and at KU Leuven and Vrije Universiteit Brussel in Belgium. I've lived in five cities in three countries but: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KcADqxnQA_4&list=RDKcADqxnQA_4&start_radio=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">I Love L.A.</a> <a href="https://southlandlosangeles.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">My first book</a> comes out in November.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="book">
      <h2>Book</h2>

      <div class="book">
        <a class="book-cover" href="https://southlandlosangeles.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <picture>
            <source srcset="/southland/cover.webp" type="image/webp">
            <img src="/southland/cover.jpg" width="1200" height="1553" loading="lazy"
                 alt="Cover of Visions of the Southland: A Year in Los Angeles County">
          </picture>
        </a>

        <div class="book-text">
          <h3><cite>Visions of the Southland: A Year in Los Angeles County</cite></h3>
          <p class="meta">Edited by Wade Graham and William Deverell, maps by Ezra Rawitsch. University of Chicago Press, 30 November 2026.</p>
          <p>Thirty-six essays trace a single year in Los Angeles County, its glitter and its grit, from water and air to music, prisons, transit, and art, by writers including Gustavo Arellano, Lynell George, Christopher Hawthorne, Carolina A. Miranda, Susan Straight, and David L. Ulin. I researched and designed the book's thirty maps, grounding each essay in the County's rivers and faults, its fires and freeways, and the patterns you can't otherwise see.</p>
          <p><a href="https://southlandlosangeles.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">More about the book at southlandlosangeles.com</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>

